There are problems with this suggestion. The ones that spring to mind 
are:
1) Using a threaded view in high traffic news groups you can easily 
have a message seperated from it's parent by hundreds of postings, 
heck, your message is 15+ postings from it's oldest text and this isn't 
a particulary busy thread. This means that for anyone without a "get 
parent" ability "glancing up" can be a pain.
2) You can't assume that the parent message will even be avaible on 
someones usenet server. For example, Boudewijn Waijers has a tendency 
to respond to posts that have timed out on the server that I use.
3) Messages are sometimes intentionally set not to show up (Killfiles), 
and in my experience responces to these message don't always thread 
properly (eg. My copy of Xnews starts a new thread for a message in 
responce to someone I've killfiled.).

I'm sure there are others.


